that happens to billionaires,

00:17:51.503 --> 00:17:52.604
and I've noticed this,

00:17:52.604 --> 00:17:53.539
I've known a lot of billionaires

00:17:53.539 --> 00:17:54.873
and they never stop talking.

00:17:54.873 --> 00:17:56.675
They never listen
to a Word you say.

00:17:56.675 --> 00:18:00.412
And they basically,
the principle is,
if you are so smart

00:18:00.412 --> 00:18:01.880
why aren't you a billionaire?

00:18:01.880 --> 00:18:03.549 align:start size:97% position:3%
Why should I listen to you
when I have a billion dollars?

00:18:03.549 --> 00:18:04.983
And they sit around

00:18:04.983 --> 00:18:08.053 align:start size:97% position:3%
and they really do make these
big plans for the world,

00:18:08.053 --> 00:18:10.622 align:start size:94% position:6%
without anybody ever
saying to them, you know,

00:18:10.622 --> 00:18:12.724
you invented a gizmo that
made you a billionaire

00:18:12.724 --> 00:18:14.059 align:start size:84% position:16%
and that's great
and congratulations,

00:18:14.059 --> 00:18:16.028 align:start size:84% position:16%
but what on earth
gave you the license

00:18:16.028 --> 00:18:17.596 align:start size:84% position:16%
to control the lives
of other people?

00:18:17.596 --> 00:18:20.599
You know, why are you flying
to Davos in your private jet

00:18:20.599 --> 00:18:23.469
to discuss how much gas I
can use in my Volkswagen?

00:18:23.469 --> 00:18:24.703
You know?

00:18:24.703 --> 00:18:27.439 align:start size:84% position:16%
It's like, it's a
complete disconnect.

00:18:27.439 --> 00:18:30.876
And so what I wanted to do, the
character of Cameron Winter,

00:18:30.876 --> 00:18:33.212
who first made his appearance
in "When Christmas Comes,"

00:18:33.212 --> 00:18:35.848
which we did talk about,
that was the original,

00:18:35.848 --> 00:18:37.483
his original story.

00:18:37.483 --> 00:18:40.419
And he really kind of
caught my imagination.

00:18:40.419 --> 00:18:43.155
And for the first time in my
life, literally, I thought,

00:18:43.155 --> 00:18:45.991
here's a character I
can build a series on.

00:18:45.991 --> 00:18:48.160
Because he's a very complex guy

00:18:48.160 --> 00:18:50.095 align:start size:97% position:3%
with a past that's
different than his present,

00:18:50.095 --> 00:18:52.297 align:start position:0%
and a future that he hopes will
be different than his past.

00:18:52.297 --> 00:18:54.333
He's kind of moving in
a certain direction,

00:18:54.333 --> 00:18:56.268 align:start size:84% position:16%
and he's surrounded
by this world

00:18:56.268 --> 00:18:58.637 align:start size:94% position:6%
that's really kind of
coming apart at the seams.

00:18:58.637 --> 00:19:00.005
So, it's the story of a man

00:19:00.005 --> 00:19:02.641 align:start size:84% position:16%
who's trying to learn
to be a good man

00:19:02.641 --> 00:19:04.443
after a past that's not so good,

00:19:04.443 --> 00:19:05.711
in a world that's collapsing.

00:19:05.711 --> 00:19:06.945
In a world that cannot supply

00:19:06.945 --> 00:19:08.780 align:start size:84% position:16%
in the values he
needs to move forward.

00:19:08.780 --> 00:19:10.048
And that to me just seemed

00:19:10.048 --> 00:19:12.050
like an endlessly
fascinating idea.

00:19:12.050 --> 00:19:14.887
So, I wanted to put him up
against one of these guys

00:19:14.887 --> 00:19:17.756
where he basically, you know,

00:19:17.756 --> 00:19:19.758
the people who get in
his way get canceled,

00:19:19.758 --> 00:19:21.860
but they get canceled
forever, you know.

00:19:23.061 --> 00:19:24.596
And so you have a guy
who's kind of looking,

00:19:24.596 --> 00:19:26.732 align:start size:94% position:6%
who has done some of this
wet work in the past.

00:19:26.732 --> 00:19:29.334
He's done some of the
kind of evil things

00:19:29.334 --> 00:19:33.038 align:start size:97% position:3%
that people have to do in
government and in espionage.

00:19:33.038 --> 00:19:35.574
And now he's thinking, "No,
I wanna live a better life."

00:19:35.574 --> 00:19:37.643
But he notices that
people around him

00:19:37.643 --> 00:19:39.778 align:start size:84% position:16%
are starting to do
those kinds of things,

00:19:39.778 --> 00:19:41.947
almost without any
conscience at all.

00:19:41.947 --> 00:19:44.616
So basically this is
two men facing off.

00:19:44.616 --> 00:19:46.518
I mean, if you picture
it as a movie poster,

00:19:46.518 --> 00:19:49.488
it would just be these two
faces looking at one another.

00:19:49.488 --> 00:19:52.658 align:start size:94% position:6%
Gerald Byrne and this
kind of English professor.

00:19:52.658 --> 00:19:54.092
That's what he is now.

00:19:54.092 --> 00:19:55.027 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he keeps telling
people, that's what I am,

00:19:55.027 --> 00:19:56.261
I'm an English professor.

00:19:56.261 --> 00:19:57.296
But he's an English
professor with a past

00:19:57.296 --> 00:19:58.730
that's much more difficult.

00:19:58.730 --> 00:20:00.499
So I wanted to put them
off against one another.

00:20:00.499 --> 00:20:03.268 align:start size:94% position:6%
Person who believes in the
traditions of the past,

00:20:03.268 --> 00:20:04.803 align:start size:88% position:13%
the art of the past,
the culture of the past,

00:20:04.803 --> 00:20:06.905 align:start size:84% position:16%
who's trying to
build a personality

00:20:06.905 --> 00:20:09.241
based on some of those
traditions and values,

00:20:09.241 --> 00:20:12.477 align:start size:97% position:3%
against a guy who basically
has reached a point.

00:20:12.477 --> 00:20:15.214 align:start size:88% position:13%
He's not a bad man, he's
just a man insulated

00:20:17.149 --> 00:20:19.117 align:start size:84% position:16%
from the consequences
of his ideas.

00:20:19.117 --> 00:20:20.719
And so I wanted these guys,

00:20:20.719 --> 00:20:21.954
two guys, to face off,

00:20:21.954 --> 00:20:23.855
and they face off with
a woman between them

00:20:23.855 --> 00:20:25.724
who is really one of
the best characters

00:20:25.724 --> 00:20:27.025
I think I've ever written.

00:20:27.025 --> 00:20:28.994
He's just an actual good woman

00:20:28.994 --> 00:20:30.796 align:start size:84% position:16%
who is married to this
guy, Gerald Byrne.

00:20:30.796 --> 00:20:33.565 align:start size:97% position:3%
And the question is, how much
of what he's doing is she

00:20:33.565 --> 00:20:34.967 align:start size:84% position:16%
involved in?
- You know, it's so

00:20:34.967 --> 00:20:36.969 align:start size:97% position:3%
interesting that you
mentioned the way these people

00:20:36.969 --> 00:20:40.505 align:start size:97% position:3%
become insulated and how
they think, because you know,

00:20:40.505 --> 00:20:42.207 align:start size:88% position:13%
I've gotten to know
Peter Thiel quite a bit,

00:20:42.207 --> 00:20:44.209
and I heard him give a talk once

00:20:44.209 --> 00:20:48.447
where he said that "When
these guys go to Davos,

00:20:48.447 --> 00:20:50.782
and to these massive meetings

00:20:50.782 --> 00:20:52.918
where they're in
essence discussing

00:20:52.918 --> 00:20:54.486
how to organize the world,"

00:20:54.486 --> 00:20:57.623
he said that "No one's ever
representing the individual.

00:20:57.623 --> 00:21:00.459 align:start position:0%
That it's always that, oh, it's
a corporation that's there,

00:21:00.459 --> 00:21:02.394
and it's a bank that's there,

00:21:02.394 --> 00:21:04.630 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it's this
conglomerate that's there.

00:21:04.630 --> 00:21:06.598
No one is representing the guy

00:21:06.598 --> 00:21:09.234
who has to put the gas in
the Volkswagen, no one."

00:21:09.234 --> 00:21:10.936
So I would say he probably is

00:21:10.936 --> 00:21:14.139
maybe the exception to the
rule, on that sort of thing.

00:21:14.139 --> 00:21:19.144
But to broadly speak, it's
like what does Bill Gates,

00:21:19.144 --> 00:21:21.413
why does he have the right to
tell us we have to eat bugs

00:21:21.413 --> 00:21:24.616 align:start position:0%
while he's now the largest farm
owner in the United States?

00:21:25.651 --> 00:21:27.319
- It is quite remarkable.

00:21:27.319 --> 00:21:28.887
Remarkable the detachment

00:21:28.887 --> 00:21:32.691 align:start position:0%
with which they exclude
themselves from their own rules.

00:21:32.691 --> 00:21:34.326
You know, there is a reason

00:21:34.326 --> 00:21:36.428 align:start size:84% position:16%
they built guillotines
in the old days.

00:21:36.428 --> 00:21:39.498 align:start size:97% position:3%
And I think that these guys
kind of exemplify that reason.

00:21:39.498 --> 00:21:42.100
I'm a very deeply opposed
to political violence,

00:21:42.100 --> 00:21:44.336
but giving these guys a good
swift kick in the backside

00:21:44.336 --> 00:21:45.637
would not be a bad idea.

00:21:46.571 --> 00:21:47.572
I don't wanna kill anybody,

00:21:47.572 --> 00:21:48.874
but just to humiliate

00:21:48.874 --> 00:21:50.042 align:start size:81% position:19%
them a little bit
- Well,

00:21:50.042 --> 00:21:51.543 align:start size:88% position:13%
now I know what
- would be a good thing.

00:21:51.543 --> 00:21:52.444 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Clip Media Matters is
gonna find of today's show.

00:21:52.444 --> 00:21:54.212
(laughing)

00:21:54.212 --> 00:21:55.380
Well done Andrew.

00:21:56.748 --> 00:21:58.350
- Bloodshed, I just
want my footprint

00:21:58.350 --> 00:22:01.320
on the seat of their pants.

00:22:01.320 --> 00:22:03.522 align:start size:88% position:13%
- Do you find that
sort of amazing though,

00:22:03.522 --> 00:22:05.824
really like just at
a granular level,

00:22:05.824 --> 00:22:07.793 align:start size:84% position:16%
that these people
have now infiltrated

00:22:07.793 --> 00:22:09.528
every part of our lives?

00:22:09.528 --> 00:22:10.996
Whether we know it or not,

00:22:10.996 --> 00:22:13.332 align:start size:97% position:3%
whether it's because you
buy all your stuff on Amazon

00:22:13.332 --> 00:22:17.502
or because Gates owns all the
land or whatever it might be,

00:22:17.502 --> 00:22:19.037 align:start size:84% position:16%
that we're all holding
this in our pocket

00:22:19.037 --> 00:22:22.741
and God knows who's in charge
of this thing at this point?

00:22:22.741 --> 00:22:23.909
- You know, there are two things

00:22:23.909 --> 00:22:25.177
that keep me from being amazed.

00:22:25.177 --> 00:22:26.578
One is all throughout history

00:22:26.578 --> 00:22:27.813
there have been
people like this.

00:22:27.813 --> 00:22:30.349
People who think, that
have these global ideas

00:22:30.349 --> 00:22:32.050
and they think that they
are going to impose them

00:22:32.050 --> 00:22:33.819 align:start size:97% position:3%
on the world, and the world's
gonna be a better place.

00:22:33.819 --> 00:22:35.987
Always a disaster
every single time.

00:22:35.987 --> 00:22:37.289
But there's also something else,

00:22:37.289 --> 00:22:40.525 align:start size:84% position:16%
the technological
age has raised people

00:22:40.525 --> 00:22:44.463 align:start size:97% position:3%
who are essentially autistic
to the level of kings.

00:22:44.463 --> 00:22:45.864
And these are guys

00:22:45.864 --> 00:22:48.133 align:start size:97% position:3%
who are completely detached
from the inner life

00:22:48.133 --> 00:22:49.668
of other human beings.

00:22:49.668 --> 00:22:52.504 align:start size:97% position:3%
I don't know if you saw that
clip of somebody at Davos

00:22:52.504 --> 00:22:55.374 align:start size:97% position:3%
saying we can make
medicines that we can track

00:22:55.374 --> 00:22:56.608
after you take them.

00:22:56.608 --> 00:22:58.744 align:start size:84% position:16%
And he said, imagine
the compliance.

00:22:58.744 --> 00:23:01.480
Well that's a guy who
has lost all sense

00:23:01.480 --> 00:23:03.014
that you and I have inner lives

00:23:03.014 --> 00:23:04.683
that are equally
important to his.

00:23:04.683 --> 00:23:06.618 align:start size:94% position:6%
And in fact, the homeless
guy on the corner

00:23:06.618 --> 00:23:08.820
has an inner life that's
equally important to mine.

00:23:08.820 --> 00:23:10.989 align:start size:97% position:3%
- I think you're talking
about Yuval, what's his name?

00:23:10.989 --> 00:23:12.858 align:start size:81% position:19%
Yuval Harari I
think is his name.

00:23:12.858 --> 00:23:14.092
- Yeah, I think
that's who it is.

00:23:14.092 --> 00:23:16.194
Noah Yuval Harari,
something like that.

00:23:16.194 --> 00:23:17.396 align:start size:88% position:13%
- I don't think that
was the guy in the clip,

00:23:17.396 --> 00:23:19.998
but he's one of these
people definitely.

00:23:19.998 --> 00:23:22.033 align:start size:97% position:3%
They can all understand
the inner lives of animals.

00:23:22.033 --> 00:23:23.568
They love animals,

00:23:23.568 --> 00:23:25.203
but they can't understand
the inner lives of people.

00:23:25.203 --> 00:23:27.839
And I think that
the technological
age we're living in

00:23:27.839 --> 00:23:30.275 align:start size:84% position:16%
has lifted those
people to new heights.

00:23:30.275 --> 00:23:33.011
They've always been around,
but now they are the guy.

00:23:33.011 --> 00:23:35.947 align:start size:84% position:16%
It's not the guy
who dug an oil well,

00:23:35.947 --> 00:23:37.149
and then made so much money

00:23:37.149 --> 00:23:38.884
that he could build
an oil business.

00:23:38.884 --> 00:23:40.118
It's not that guy.

00:23:40.118 --> 00:23:42.354
It's not the guy who
came from overseas

00:23:42.354 --> 00:23:46.024
and built a movie studio, and
had his hands on the film,

00:23:46.024 --> 00:23:48.160 align:start size:84% position:16%
and then could hire
other people to do it.

00:23:48.160 --> 00:23:50.429
These are guys who deal
with little, you know,

00:23:50.429 --> 00:23:53.698 align:start size:84% position:16%
Os and ones, and
really have never had

00:23:53.698 --> 00:23:57.335 align:start size:97% position:3%
the experience of another
human being mattering to them

00:23:57.335 --> 00:23:59.638
at the level that people
have to matter to you,

00:23:59.638 --> 00:24:02.874 align:start size:97% position:3%
when you are in charge of
large areas of human beings.

00:24:02.874 --> 00:24:05.076 align:start size:97% position:3%
- It's funny, do you
remember a couple months back

00:24:05.076 --> 00:24:06.311
when Mark Zuckerberg

00:24:06.311 --> 00:24:08.747 align:start size:88% position:13%
was introducing the
metaverse to everybody,

00:24:08.747 --> 00:24:11.082 align:start size:84% position:16%
and he's in the
commercial himself,

00:24:11.082 --> 00:24:13.351 align:start size:94% position:6%
and he's walking into
this alternative universe

00:24:13.351 --> 00:24:14.820
and it's like, first off,

00:24:14.820 --> 00:24:18.557 align:start position:0%
you're the guy who runs Facebook
who has screwed up so much

00:24:18.557 --> 00:24:20.659
of how we feel about
each other these days,

00:24:20.659 --> 00:24:23.361 align:start size:84% position:16%
and has caused parents
to hate children,

00:24:23.361 --> 00:24:24.930
and friends to turn on each
other, and everything else.

00:24:24.930 --> 00:24:26.698
You also seem like an automaton.

00:24:26.698 --> 00:24:27.966
You don't even seem
like a full human.

00:24:27.966 --> 00:24:29.434
And now I'm gonna follow you

00:24:29.434 --> 00:24:31.903 align:start size:84% position:16%
into your crazy
alternate universe?

00:24:31.903 --> 00:24:34.573
And yet we know that a
huge percentage of people

00:24:34.573 --> 00:24:35.407
are gonna do it.

00:24:36.441 --> 00:24:38.777
- Yeah, well, one of the things

00:24:38.777 --> 00:24:41.847
that I think is important to
realize is that many people,

00:24:41.847 --> 00:24:44.182
many more people than you
think, are mentally ill.

00:24:44.182 --> 00:24:45.684
A larger percentage of people

00:24:45.684 --> 00:24:46.618
than you think.
- Oh I think it's

00:24:46.618 --> 00:24:48.119
quite a high number, actually.

00:24:48.119 --> 00:24:49.821
- It's a high number, and
it wouldn't surprise me

00:24:49.821 --> 00:24:51.656
if it were 50%.
- I'm on Twitter.

00:24:51.656 --> 00:24:52.824
(laughing)

00:24:52.824 --> 00:24:53.758
- Well, there you go.

00:24:53.758 --> 00:24:55.627
I mean, it really is interesting

00:24:55.627 --> 00:24:57.863
that they're not
dealing with life

00:24:57.863 --> 00:24:59.931
in a very connected way.

00:24:59.931 --> 00:25:02.667 align:start size:97% position:3%
You know, all this stuff about
the golden rule, you know,

00:25:02.667 --> 00:25:04.236
do unto unto others as
you would have them do,

00:25:04.236 --> 00:25:06.137
love your neighbor as yourself.

00:25:06.137 --> 00:25:08.073
That kind of idea.

00:25:08.073 --> 00:25:09.541
There's a reason for
that kind of idea.

00:25:09.541 --> 00:25:11.510 align:start size:97% position:3%
It's not because you're a
good boy and you go to heaven

00:25:11.510 --> 00:25:13.044 align:start size:88% position:13%
if you love your
neighbor like yourself,

00:25:13.044 --> 00:25:15.280 align:start size:88% position:13%
it's because it
connects you to reality.

00:25:15.280 --> 00:25:16.681
It connects you to the world

00:25:16.681 --> 00:25:20.018
and to this infinite
pattern of human beings

00:25:20.018 --> 00:25:21.219
interacting with each other,

00:25:21.219 --> 00:25:22.921
which is all of the joy of life.

00:25:22.921 --> 00:25:24.789 align:start size:94% position:6%
You get it in your family
with your children,

00:25:24.789 --> 00:25:26.825
you get it in your marriage,

00:25:26.825 --> 00:25:28.326
but also you can get it
in your neighborhood.

00:25:28.326 --> 00:25:31.596 align:start size:97% position:3%
And all of that stuff is
being dissected and destroyed

00:25:31.596 --> 00:25:35.734 align:start position:0%
by people who do not experience
the inner lives of others

00:25:35.734 --> 00:25:38.436 align:start size:97% position:3%
because they're essentially,
at least morally,

00:25:38.436 --> 00:25:40.105
I don't wanna make it
a medical diagnosis,

00:25:40.105 --> 00:25:41.540
but morally autistic.

00:25:41.540 --> 00:25:44.409 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I think as Zuckerberg
is a great example.

00:25:44.409 --> 00:25:45.944
- Do you think there's
a way to reverse that?

00:25:45.944 --> 00:25:47.412
I mean, I do sense

00:25:47.412 --> 00:25:50.749 align:start size:97% position:3%
that there's gonna be a
real anti-technology revolt,

00:25:50.749 --> 00:25:52.817 align:start size:84% position:16%
at some point within
the next decade.

00:25:52.817 --> 00:25:54.953
I mean, it's just so obvious.

00:25:54.953 --> 00:25:57.355 align:start size:88% position:13%
The level of censorship
and shadow banning,

00:25:57.355 --> 00:25:59.591
and don't talk about
Hunter Biden laptop.

00:25:59.591 --> 00:26:00.959 align:start size:81% position:19%
You can't question
this election.

00:26:00.959 --> 00:26:02.460
You can question that one.

00:26:02.460 --> 00:26:04.996
Like all the asymmetries
of it and inconsistencies,

00:26:04.996 --> 00:26:08.233
I think on top of just the
general endless scrolling,

00:26:08.233 --> 00:26:10.368 align:start size:94% position:6%
and what it's doing to
the dopamine in our brains

00:26:10.368 --> 00:26:11.836
and all of this stuff.

00:26:11.836 --> 00:26:14.039 align:start size:97% position:3%
I sense there's gonna be like
a real push against this.

00:26:14.039 --> 00:26:15.407 align:start size:84% position:16%
Do you think that
that's probably right?

00:26:15.407 --> 00:26:17.642
- Yes, I completely
agree with that.

00:26:17.642 --> 00:26:20.779
And the reason is because
it's happened in the past

00:26:20.779 --> 00:26:22.447 align:start size:84% position:16%
during the Industrial
Revolution.

00:26:22.447 --> 00:26:23.582
These factories were built.

00:26:23.582 --> 00:26:25.183
They destroyed families.

00:26:25.183 --> 00:26:27.118 align:start size:84% position:16%
Suddenly children
who used to stay home

00:26:27.118 --> 00:26:28.587
and help you with the farm,

00:26:28.587 --> 00:26:30.088 align:start size:97% position:3%
