And the fact that you
just said, and I know,

00:44:05.576 --> 00:44:07.845 align:start size:97% position:3%
'cause I spoke to Spencer
and Josh before the wedding,

00:44:07.845 --> 00:44:09.580
that they invited people

00:44:09.580 --> 00:44:12.616
who are not personally
okay with gay marriage.

00:44:12.616 --> 00:44:14.852
It's like, do you think
that those people left

00:44:14.852 --> 00:44:16.820
maybe a little bit
more open-minded?

00:44:16.820 --> 00:44:19.456 align:start size:97% position:3%
Probably, as opposed to just
being called homophobes,

00:44:19.456 --> 00:44:20.658
and not invited.

00:44:20.658 --> 00:44:22.292 align:start size:84% position:16%
Then which way would
they be tilting?

00:44:22.292 --> 00:44:26.730
- Well, exactly, and it's so
dumb, I mean, it's so dumb.

00:44:26.730 --> 00:44:28.232 align:start size:81% position:19%
If your idea of
your philosophy is

00:44:28.232 --> 00:44:29.600
there are people
who agree with me,

00:44:29.600 --> 00:44:31.068 align:start size:84% position:16%
and then there are
people who are racist,

00:44:31.068 --> 00:44:33.370
sexist, phobic of some
sort, you're an idiot.

00:44:33.370 --> 00:44:34.905
I mean, you're an idiot.

00:44:34.905 --> 00:44:36.140
All of us have ideas.

00:44:36.140 --> 00:44:38.175 align:start size:81% position:19%
- But enough about
Kamala Harris.

00:44:38.175 --> 00:44:40.444
(laughing)

00:44:40.444 --> 00:44:41.612
- That's beyond idiocy.

00:44:43.047 --> 00:44:45.649
But no, obviously if you're
gonna have a conversation,

00:44:45.649 --> 00:44:48.552 align:start size:94% position:6%
you have to make room
for other people's ideas.

00:44:48.552 --> 00:44:50.521 align:start size:84% position:16%
Even if those ideas
make you angry.

00:44:50.521 --> 00:44:52.990
You have to be able to see
what people of goodwill,

00:44:52.990 --> 00:44:54.525
some people are not
people of goodwill,

00:44:54.525 --> 00:44:56.493 align:start size:84% position:16%
but people of
goodwill, disagree.

00:44:56.493 --> 00:44:58.062 align:start size:81% position:19%
And you have to
let them disagree,

00:44:58.062 --> 00:44:59.296 align:start size:84% position:16%
and you have to see
what they have to say.

00:44:59.296 --> 00:45:01.699
I think that Christian right

00:45:01.699 --> 00:45:04.768 align:start size:97% position:3%
has a lot to say about gender
that's not being heard,

00:45:04.768 --> 00:45:05.736
that we should listen to,

00:45:05.736 --> 00:45:07.404
because obviously the opposite

00:45:07.404 --> 00:45:09.540
of what they're doing is a mess.

00:45:09.540 --> 00:45:11.375
But, that doesn't
necessarily mean

00:45:11.375 --> 00:45:14.378
I have to set people on fire
when I disagree with them.

00:45:14.378 --> 00:45:17.281
It doesn't mean that I have
to destroy them or hate them.

00:45:17.281 --> 00:45:18.849
And I think in this case,

00:45:18.849 --> 00:45:21.385 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean this was
something I was on board.

00:45:21.385 --> 00:45:23.787 align:start position:0%
People always say that I changed
my mind because of Spencer,

00:45:23.787 --> 00:45:25.823
but that's just
a simple untruth.

00:45:25.823 --> 00:45:28.559
I always felt this
way, that being gay

00:45:28.559 --> 00:45:31.762 align:start size:97% position:3%
is a very specific thing,
it's not a choice people make.

00:45:31.762 --> 00:45:35.365 align:start size:84% position:16%
People have died
and been imprisoned
because they were gay.

00:45:36.533 --> 00:45:38.335
It's not something you
wake up in the morning,

00:45:38.335 --> 00:45:39.837 align:start size:81% position:19%
or you're a little
kid and think,

00:45:39.837 --> 00:45:42.339
"I want to grow up to be gay,"
that's not the way it works.

00:45:42.339 --> 00:45:44.241
It is something that people are,

00:45:44.241 --> 00:45:47.678
and it comes with a
lot of ramifications

00:45:47.678 --> 00:45:50.481
that are worth talking about
between people of good will.

00:45:50.481 --> 00:45:52.649 align:start size:84% position:16%
I mean, when I hear
Christians say,

00:45:52.649 --> 00:45:55.219
"Well it's okay as long
as they're celibate."

00:45:55.219 --> 00:45:57.321
Yeah, it's okay with me as
long as you're celibate.

00:45:57.321 --> 00:45:59.289 align:start size:69% position:31%
- Yeah.
(laughing)

00:45:59.289 --> 00:46:01.425 align:start size:88% position:13%
- How about you try
that and get back to me.

00:46:02.993 --> 00:46:06.563
I think just a little bit of,
I hate to use the word love,

00:46:06.563 --> 00:46:08.398
like it matters,
but it does matter.

00:46:08.398 --> 00:46:09.867
A little bit of love between us,

00:46:09.867 --> 00:46:13.570 align:start size:97% position:3%
a little bit of compassion
for each person's sensibility,

00:46:13.570 --> 00:46:15.405
and then you can start
to trust one another

00:46:15.405 --> 00:46:20.043 align:start size:97% position:3%
to discuss things at a
level beyond bile, you know,

00:46:20.043 --> 00:46:22.880 align:start size:88% position:13%
a level beyond
sloganeering and hatred.

00:46:22.880 --> 00:46:24.214
I think these are
important issues.

00:46:24.214 --> 00:46:26.350 align:start size:88% position:13%
I think gender is a
hugely important issue.

00:46:26.350 --> 00:46:28.385 align:start size:84% position:16%
I think it's a
hugely complex issue,

00:46:28.385 --> 00:46:30.554
but that doesn't mean you
take a 16 year old girl

00:46:30.554 --> 00:46:32.489
and cut her breasts off.

00:46:32.489 --> 00:46:36.226
You have to have decades of
conversation and philosophy

00:46:36.226 --> 00:46:38.929 align:start size:97% position:3%
before you even think about
making moves like that.

00:46:38.929 --> 00:46:40.264
And we just don't do it anymore

00:46:40.264 --> 00:46:41.899
because our press is so corrupt,

00:46:41.899 --> 00:46:45.035 align:start size:97% position:3%
and our academies are so
corrupt, and our government,

00:46:45.035 --> 00:46:46.603 align:start size:81% position:19%
and our businesses
are so corrupt,

00:46:46.603 --> 00:46:50.007
that they have basically
shut the conversation down.

00:46:50.007 --> 00:46:52.042
- Andrew, you are
a true professional

00:46:52.042 --> 00:46:54.311 align:start size:84% position:16%
who knows how to close
down an interview.

00:46:54.311 --> 00:46:56.079
You're a great gal, by the way.

00:46:56.079 --> 00:47:00.017 align:start size:97% position:3%
